ptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 AUG 98 at 09 14 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast lump  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of breast tissue with a localizing wire entering the lateral superficial portion  The specimen is entirely inked black and posterior surface is overinked blue  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm firm  white stellate mass with fibrous extensions located  0 5cm from the posterior margin  and abutting the superficial margin  Sectioning through the remaining breast parenchyma reveals rubbery white fibrous tissue with a small amount of adipose tissue  Representative sections are submitted  Section code  A B  Mass to closest posterior margin  inked blue  and closest superficial margin  inked red   C  Section of remaining breast parenchyma overinked in red  D  Representative section from remaining breast parenchyma  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  final superficial lateral margin  is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  One side of the specimen is inked black  the opposing side is inked blue  Sectioning reveals predominantly adipose tissue with a small amount of soft gray white fibrous tissue  There is a 