e results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  02 MAY 95 at 15 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm yellow red lumpectomy specimen with a localizing wire in place  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm irregular firm  tan to red area suspicious for invasive carcinoma  No frozen section is done because the nodule is too small  The nodule comes to within 0 2cm of the closest inked resection margin grossly  The nodule is submitted in cassettes A and B with the remainder of the specimen in cassettes C  D  and E  Resident  RICHARD S  HAMILTON  HMS     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST  LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  Ajit J  Alles  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   LUMPECTOMY , Positive.
