Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Breast CTR Surg WAC 240 MEEI MRN  REMOVED_DATE Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  CONNIE ROCHE  NP KENNY C LAI  M D  RACHEL ANN HITT  M D  Resident  Matija Snuderl  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D  CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 56 year old woman with very dense breast with indeterminate focus of enhancement seen in the medial left breast on MRI  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  A  BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY 1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  WELL DIFFERENTIATED GRADE REMOVED_DATE 2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  DCIS   MICROPAPILLARY TYPE  GRADE REMOVED_DATE 3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH APOCRINE METAPLASIA  SEE NOTE  Note  Sections of the core biopsy reveal a rare cluster of angulated ducts infiltrating the stroma which are present over an area measuring approximately 0 2cm  Adjacent to the lesion is a 0 3cm cluster of ducts which are expanded by a proliferation of monomorphic ductal cells arranged in a micropapillary pattern lining the duct structures  The morphologic findings are compatible with a diagnosis of invasive tubular carcinoma arising in association with low grade micropapillary ductal carcinoma in situ  To help confirm these diagnoses  we performed level sections and a panel of immunostains on the core biopsy  Multiple level sections show the DCIS to better advantage  An immunostain for keratin REMOVED_DATE shows focal loss of staining in luminal cells and supports the diagnosis of DCIS  Immunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin  p63  myosin and calponin performed on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  demonstrate absence of the myoepithelial layer in the infiltrating ducts and supports the diagnosis of invasive ductal carcinoma  Overall  the findings are limited due to limited sampling of the lesion  however  based on morphology and immunohistochemistry  the findings are compatible with well differentiated invasive ductal carcinoma and low grade ductal carcinoma in situ  Dr  David Wilbur has reviewed this case and concurs with the diagnosis  GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen is received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN only is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm  aggregate of multiple tan yellow to gray white fibroadipose tissue cores  which are submitted in toto  in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on Monday August 31   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 12 51 13PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART   Breast  Left    Core biopsy  report_end  , Not_Done.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 MAY 94 ACCESSIONED ON  24 MAY 94 at 14 28 CLINICAL DATA  Mass by mammogram and palpation                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED GRADE REMOVED_DATE   95    REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO WITHIN LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM OF AN INKED MARGIN  AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CRIBIFORM TYPE   5     SEE NOTE   NOTE  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  The results on estrogen and progesterone receptor studies will be reported in an addendum  Diagnosis by  Volker Nickeleit  M D  Signed On  26 MAY 94 at 14 19                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 MAY 94 at 07 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of breast tissue  inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 6cm in greatest dimension  ill defined  tan white  gritty and firm area that grossly abuts an inked resection margin  The remainder of the specimen is predominantly composed of unremarkable breast and adipose tissue  A representative section of the lesion is frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  Representative sections of remainder of the specimen submitted in cassettes A through J  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST MASS   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Essam Ahmed  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Positive.
