Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  23 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  23 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 12 13 CLINICAL DATA  74 y o  female with breast carcinoma by fine needle aspiration undergoing right modified radical mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  INVASING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of the tumor  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 7 OF 8 LYMPH NODES AND IN AXILLARY SOFT TISSUE  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA  SPECIMEN  1   EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   ADDITIONAL    EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 5 OF 5 LYMPH NODES AND IN AXILLARY VEINS  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 49                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 42 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right axillary node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tissue fragment with a 0 8cm firm lymph node  The node is sectioned to reveal a white tan  firm cut surface  Half the node is frozen as FX 1  and saved frozen  The remainder is submitted in cassette A  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  additional axillary nodes  right  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm aggregate of adipose tissue from which lymph nodes are dissected and submitted in cassettes B through C  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  right modified radical mastectomy   is a modified radical mastectomy specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x 22 x 4 5cm  with an attached axilla of  14 x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0 cm and an overlying skin ellipse measuring  23 x 11cm   containing an eccentric nipple  4 0cm in diameter  7 7cm away from the medial end of the skin ellipse  The nipple areola complex is grossly unremarkable  No scars are grossly identified in the overlying skin ellipse  The deep resection margin consist of a smooth fascial plane  The specimen is inked black and the axillary contents are removed  A lymph node dissection is performed  The main mastectomy specimen is then serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm firm  gritty area with a stellate border that comes to within 0 8cm of the deep  closest  margin  The inferior margin is 2 0cm away  and the superior margin is 2 5cm away from the mass  SECTION CODE  D L  Axillary lymph nodes  M  Mass  in relation to deep margin  N  Closest inferior margin  O  Deep margin  P Q  Representative sections of tumor nodules  R  Representative section of normal breast parenchyma away from mass lesion  Resident  JUSTIN M  CATES  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS 1  LYMPH NODE  METASTATIC CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  RUBEN D  CARRASCO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION PART B  RIGHT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART C  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   ADDITIONAL    EXCISION   report_end  , Positive.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  31 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  31 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 11 44 CLINICAL DATA  Question invasive carcinoma  Margins please                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  50   SEE NOTE   INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  50    FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH CYST FORMATION AND SCLEROSING ADENOSIS   MICROCALCIFICATIONS  BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL LATERAL AND POSTERIOR MARGINS   EXCISION  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor measures 1 1cm in greatest diameter  It involves the deep margin  The specimen designated   additional lateral and posterior margins   is involved with infiltrating ductal carcinoma  10   and intraductal carcinoma  90   on one edge  but it does not extend through the specimen  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION  FIFTEEN LYMPH NODES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA  LEVEL II   EXCISION  TWO LYMPH NODES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 16                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 07 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 7cm piece of breast tissue with an attached ellipse of skin which measures REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  There is a short silk suture at the superior margin and a long silk suture at the lateral margin  The specimen is inked  anterior designated yellow  and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm poorly defined  white  firm  gritty area which involves the deep margin and comes to within 0 8cm of the inferior margin  A representative section of the deep resection margin is frozen as FS 1 and saved frozen  A representative section of the inferior resection margin is frozen as FS 3  now A  Representative serial sections from lateral to medial are submitted in B through H  with B through E being the lateral half and the remainder being the medial half  Labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  right breast additional lateral and posterior margins   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal fibrous tissue with multiple cysts up to 0 3cm  Submitted entirely in I through S  Labeled  right axilla nodes   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of fatty tissue  from which multiple tan  rubbery lymph nodes  ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 1 0cm are dissected  portions of these lymph nodes are submitted in T through V  Labeled  Level II   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of fatty tissue  from which two lymph nodes  each 0 3cm  is dissected  The nodes are submitted in W  and the remainder in X  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 2  BREAST RIGHT  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING   INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  SOME IS COMEDO  TYPE   CARCINOMA APPROACHES TO WITHIN 0 1CM OF DEEP MARGIN  O R  Resident  RICHARD S  HAMILTON  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST TISSUE PART B  ADDITIONAL LATERAL   POSTERIOR MARGINS  RIGHT BREA PART C  AXILLA NODES  RIGHT  PART D  LEVEL II , Positive.
