Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 35 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  1 O CM BY GROSS MEASUREMENT  GRADE 2 OF 3  EXTENDING FOCALLY TO A POSTERIOR MEDIAL MARGIN  NOTE  No lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is identified  An in situ component is not seen  The other sampled margins appear free of tumor  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 00                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 58 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit nubmer  and further labeled  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm breast  inspected and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm hard  tan  well defined mass abutting the posterior medial margin which is inked in green  A representative section is frozen as FX  1  and now submitted in cassette A  The remainder of the specimen is inked as follows  Lateral and medial   red  anterior   black  posterior   green  superior   blue  B D  mass  tumor on medial margin  E  short stitch F H  unremarkable breast Resident  GARY LETTS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST MASS   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA CONSISTENT WITH DUCTAL  O R  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Paul Snowden Russell  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT  EXCISION   report_end  , Positive.
