Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 MAY 98 ACCESSIONED ON  13 MAY 98 at 09 50 CLINICAL DATA  Pregnant female  8cm mass of breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  WITH MULTIFOCAL MICROINVASION  EXTENDING TO MULTIPLE RESECTION MARGINS  Note  All blocks contain ductal carcinoma in situ  Occasional foci of stromal invasion are seen  the largest of which spans 1mm  While this particular focus is distant from resection margins  other areas suspicious for stromal invasion are close  1mm   to margins  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is seen  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  15 MAY 98 at 18 03 Consulting Pathologist s   Jacqueline Haas  MD                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 MAY 98 at 11 14 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast lump   are two portions of firm breast  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  The specimens are inked and sectioned to reveal focally firm fibrofatty tissue with multifocal white calcification with no discrete lesion  Representative sections of the smaller portion with calcifications are frozen as FX  1 and are saved for Cox 5  The remainder of the small case is entirely submitted in cassettes A B  The larger portion is entirely submitted in cassettes C H  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  COMEDO TYPE WITH CALCIFICATIONS  O R  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Suzanne B  Keel  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Negative.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 16 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA AND LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The infiltrating carcinoma is present as four microscopic foci in twenty slides  Lymphatic invasion is not identified  The examined inked margin is free of infiltrating or in situ carcinoma  however lobular carcinoma in situ is present within a fraction of one millimeter of an inked margin  The entire specimen has been submitted  Dr  Frederick Koerner has examined selected slides on this case and concurs with this diagnosis  Atypical lobular hyperplasia or LCIS is present in approximately half of the submitted slides  2  HYALINIZED CALCIFIED FIBROADENOMA  Diagnosis by  John O Connell  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 37                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Right breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x 5 x 2 8cm fragment of breast tissue with a localizing wire in place  Serial sectioning reveals a 0 4cm area of fatty  tan  gritty tissue corresponding to the terminus of the stereotactic needle biopsy  No frozen section done  The grossly suspicious areas are submitted in A and B and the remainder is submitted in C through T  Gross Description by  Elizabeth Bailey  MD Resident  Jason Lockridge  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS   RIGHT BREAST MASS  EXCISION  NO AREAS GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Michael Pins  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  John O Connell  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Positive.
