 receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 09 55 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm breast with a localizing wire in place  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm  ill defined stellate tan firm nodule present at 0 4cm from the closest surgical margin  The remaining breast tissue is unremarkable  A section of the tumor with inked margin is frozen as FX  1 and submitted in A  The remaining tissue is submitted in B and C  The neighboring sections are in D and E  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  LEFT   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  NEOPLASM IS PRESENT AT THE INKED SURGICAL MARGIN  O R  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  David M Frim  M D  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST BIOPSY   report_end  , Positive.
