rs by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 07 43 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm breast infiltrated with blue dye and entirely inked black  The superior aspect is overinked yellow  the posterior is overinked blue  the specimen is serially section from lateral to medial to reveal a 1 2cm tan gray firm mass  0 3cm from the anterior margin  1 0cm from the posterior margin  Section code  A B  Mass relative to anterior margin C  Mass relative to posterior margin D  Additional section of mass with anterior and posterior margins E  Additional section of posterior margin F  Additional normal breast parenchyma  Received fresh and  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axilla sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm piece of adipose and lymphoid tissue  which is bisected and entirely submitted in Cassettes O and P  Also received fresh and  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of adipose tissue  from which multiple lymph nodes are identified  These range from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm in greatest diameter  Representative sections of each lymph node is submitted in Cassettes Q T  Also received fresh and  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional anterior margins   are 3 pieces of fibroadipose breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm in aggregate  The tissue is unremarkable and is submitted entirely in Cassettes G H  Also received fresh and  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  final shaved margins   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm in addition to a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  which is inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast tissue  This unoriented specimens are submitted totally in Cassettes I N  Resident  SAMANTHA J  PULLIAM  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     Breast  left    Lesion suspicious for carcinoma close to the anterior margin                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  SENTINEL NODE  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION PART D  BREAST  ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR MARGINS   EXCISIONAL B PART E  BREAST  FINAL SHAVED MARGINS   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Positive.
