Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 10 CLINICAL DATA  70 year old with breast ductal carcinoma in situ    margins on wide excision                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  SINGLE MICROSCOPIC FOCUS  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  BREAST  LEFT   INFERIOR TISSUE    UNREMARKABLE FAT  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 53                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are two specimens  Otherwise unidentified is a 475 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm simple mastectomy specimen with the nipple still attached is a portion of a REMOVED_DATE x 3 7cm skin ellipse  Sutures are present on the skin ellipse  a short stitch  presumably designating superior  and a long stitch presumably designating lateral  The superficial resection margins are inked superior lateral green  superior medial red  inferomedial blue  and inferior lateral yellow  The deep resection margin is inked black  Sectioning reveals a 1 6cm hemorrhagic cyst lining 0 8cm deep to the medial end of the skin ellipse  and coming 3 5cm from the deep resection margin  This cavity is bordered by an irregular area of pale yellow tissue extending up to 0 4cm from the smooth wall of the cyst  Grossly  the cyst wall comes within 0 6cm of the inferomedial superficial resection margin and 0 8cm of the superomedial superficial resection margin  Section code  A B  cyst  representative sections C  cyst  showing closest approach to inferomedial superficial margin D  cyst  showing closest approach to superomedial superficial margin E  closest deep margin to cyst  grossly uninvolved F H  fibrotic areas in remainder of breast parenchyma Labeled  left breast  additional inferior tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm adipose tissue fragment with an unremarkable cut surface  entirely submitted in I J  Resident  DARRYL E  PALMER TOY  MD PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael J Yaremchuk  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  LEFT    INFERIOR TISSUE  , Not_Done.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  25 MAY 93 ACCESSIONED ON  25 MAY 93 at 14 33 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast lesion                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  EXTENSIVE  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  90   WITH EXTENSIVE CANCERIZATION OF LOBULES  1 6 CM IN DIAMETER  EXTENDING TO AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN  SLIDE D  AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  10    2  MICROCALCIFICATIONS  NOTE  Definite lymphatic invasion is not present  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Sigrid Regauer  MD Signed On  28 MAY 93 at 17 59 Staff Pathologist  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                      S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   1   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 372 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 3  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 12     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 MAY 93 at 09 44 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1 0cm piece of breast with a localizing wire in place  The specimen is accompanied by a specimen radiograph  The tissue is inked and sectioned  revealing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm firm  tan brown mass which abuts the inked resection margin  The remainder of the specimen consists of unremarkable adipose tissue  A representative section of the mass is frozen as Frozen Section  1 and saved frozen  BRDU studies are performed  The remainder of the tissue is submitted in B through J  Resident  Jeoffry Brennick  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Essam Ahmed  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Negative.
