Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 09 59 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE I  100   FORMING MANY TINY NODULES  PRESENT IN ALL THE SECTIONS  AND ABUTTING THE MARGINS AT SEVERAL POINTS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The largest nodule measures 0 4cm  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 38                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 34 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm portion of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue which is inked and sectioned to reveal an unremarkable breast parenchyma  None frozen  Submitted in toto in A through G  Resident  Ajit J  Alles  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  NO GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS LESION IS LARGE ENOUGH TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Positive.
