terminations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 AUG 95 at 15 17 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  is a modified radical mastectomy specimen  consisting of left breast REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm  and overlying 21 0cm skin ellipse  a 1 1cm nipple with retraction  and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm axillary tail  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm area of breast parenchyma which contains multiple  dilated ducts containing a yellow semi solid material  These dilated ducts are located beneath the nipple  extend 0 1cm from the nipple surface  0 2cm from the inferior margin  2 0cm from the superior resection margin  3 0cm from the deep resection margin  approximately 3 0cm from the medial margin and 14 0cm from the lateral margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma on cross section reveals firm  tan to gray  rubbery tissue  intermixed with adipose tissue  There is no gross evidence of invasive carcinoma  The axillary adipose tissue is dissected to reveal multiple  firm  well circumscribed  lymph nodes that range in size from 0 2cm to 1 0cm  A frozen section is performed and the frozen tissue is saved frozen  SECTION CODE  A  area of dilated ducts which extend to the closest deep margin  relative to the closest deep margin B  area of dilated ducts with paste like intraluminal material closest to superior margin C D  representative section of dilated ducts with paste like material E G  representative sections of firm rubbery breast parenchyma  H  nearest deep resection margin from firm breast tissue I  representative sections of breast parenchyma J  representative section of nipple K Q  axillary lymph nodes R  breast parenchyma  0 5cm beneath the nipple S  dilated ducts with luminal paste like material  representative sections T  lateral aspect of dilated ducts with luminal paste like material U  representative section of nipple V  inferior skin margin closest to nipple with dilated ducts  0 2cm from margin  closest to mipple  en face  W  superior skin margin  closest to nipple  en face  X  medial skin margin Y  lateral skin margin Z  dilated ducts with paste like material  medial most extension of this area AA GG  Additonal sections of breast from areas of microcalcifications  Gross Description by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT AXILLARY CONTENTS    report_end  , Negative.
