_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Note  All of the nodules grossly and histologically appear to be distinct lesions  each associated with DCIS  The morphology of the third and fourth nodules have some similarities  The first two nodules  however  have notably different morphologies from each other and from the third and fourth nodules  Tumor  1 appears slightly lower grade and has more mucin production  Tumor  2 is high grade  and the cells have abundant cytoplasm  The DCIS associated with these two nodules also has a different morphologic appearance  Taking these facts into account  the invasive carcinomas in this region of the breast most likely represent three or possibly four independent primaries  Stains for receptors  SKIN   RIGHT BREAST   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA  SENTINEL    EXCISION  TWO ISOLATED TUMOR CELLS   0 02CM  PRESENT IN ONE OUT OF TWO LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor cells are identified only on one cytokeratin stain and are not identified on HE  No extracapsular extension is identified  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right mastectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 5cm right mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm irregular overlying portion of skin   There is a centrally located unremarkable nipple measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  No scar is appreciated  There is a suture designating the 12 o clock aspect and a potential REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm portion of attached axillary tissue along the lateral aspect  The anterior aspect is inked blue and the posterior is black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal two discontinuous well delineated masses within the medial lower inner quadrant  0 5cm apart  Mass  1  more lateral mass  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and is gritty  indurated and well delineated on cut surface  Mass  1 comes to 1 5cm from the cl