Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  19 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  19 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 40 CLINICAL DATA  Known  presumed  metastatic gastric carcinoma  treated with chemotherapy  Known left breast cancer  Now with right breast mass and   left supraclavicular lymph node                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     A  BREAST  RIGHT LATERAL  1   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE CARCINOMA CONSISTENT WITH LOBULAR CARCINOMA PRESENT IN 7 OF 8 TISSUE SECTIONS  PRESENT AT MULTIPLE INKED SURFACES   SEE NOTE   2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The largest single tumor dimension on one slide is 1 4cm  However  the tumor is probably much larger since it is present in 7 of 8 tissue sections  The tumor cells are positive for ER  negative for PR and focally positive for GCDFP  Definite in situ carcinoma is not seen  The overall cytology  morphology and immunoperoxidase reactivity are consistent with invasive lobular carcinoma  However  in the absence of an in situ component  one can not completely rule out a gastric metastasis  The slides of the previous gastric carcinoma were not available for review  B  BREAST  RIGHT BREAST  2  CENTRAL   EXCISION  INVASIVE CARCINOMA CONSISTENT WITH LOBULAR CARCINOMA  MULTIFOCAL  PRESENT AT MULTIPLE INKED SURFACES   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Definite in situ component is not seen Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  C  BREAST  RIGHT ADDITIONAL MARGIN  2   EXCISION  INVASIVE CARCINOMA CONSISTENT WITH LOBULAR CARCINOMA  MULTIFOCAL  PRESENT AT THE MARGIN DESIGNATED BY THE BLACK STITCH AND THE OPPOSITE MARGIN   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The foci of carcinoma each average 0 2cm in overall dimension  Definite in situ carcinoma is not seen  D  LYMPH NODE  LEFT SUPRACLAVICULAR   EXCISION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA CONSISTENT WITH BREAST ORIGIN   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Invasive carcinoma permeates fibroadipose tissue forming a dominant mass  Definite lymph node architecture is not seen  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 03                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 03     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS  Left Supraclavicular Lymph Node   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 38     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum      LEFT SUPRACLAVICULAR LYMPH NODE   The tumor cells are focally positive for GCDFP 15  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 34     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Right   The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 12 07 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Two specimens are received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  Designated  right