 specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a stellate scar  a necrotic mass and a calcified nodule  The tan white stellate fibrotic scar in the outer quadrant  measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  lies approximately between 9 and 10 o clock position   0 1cm from the posterior inked margin and 0 3cm from overlying skin  Adjacent and abutting the stellate scar there is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 1cm tan yellow ill defined  necrotic mass which grossly abuts the nodule on the overlying skin and lies 2 5cm from posterior inked margin  Approximately 0 8cm medial to the scar in the lower quadrant  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan white fairly well circumscribed calcified nodule which lies 4cm from the posterior inked margin and 3 5cm from overlying skin  The breast parenchyma between the 2 nodules is dense white  rubbery and fibrous  The remaining breast parenchyma contains diffusely tan white rubbery nodular fibrous tissue interspersed with a moderate amount of tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue  No additional discrete masses or lesions are noted  The upper outer quadrant tissue is palpated for lymph nodes and no lymph nodes are gross appreciated  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrotic scar to include closest inked margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrotic scar to include adjacent necrotic mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Necrotic mass to overlying skin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Calcified nodule to include closest posterior inked margin submitted following decalcification   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast parenchyma  between the necrotic mass and the calcified nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Breast parenchyma  central quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous breast parenchyma  inner quadrant  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  Final Diagnosis by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 25   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 04 21 02PM ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 26   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 01 35 36PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART   Breast  Right   Simple Mastectomy  report_end  , Negative.
