r is not grossly identified  The remaining cut surface shows diffuse dense gray white fibrotic tissue  up to 40   which is primarily localized to the upper outer quadrant  Sectioning of the axillary contents reveals three probable lymph nodes  Representative sections are submitted as follows  G I  previous biopsy site J K  representative fibrous tissue L  lymph nodes Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  additional left axillary lymph node  is a 0 6cm tan pink lymph node with minimal attached tan yellow fibroadipose tissue which is submitted in toto as M  Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  DI TIAN  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART C  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLARY  , Positive.
