Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 MAY 95 ACCESSIONED ON  26 MAY 95 at 16 05 CLINICAL DATA  46 year old female with right breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  1 7 CM   GRADE REMOVED_DATE  PRESENT A FRACTION OF A MM FROM AN INKED RESECTION MARGIN   SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH FIBROSIS  MICROCYSTS  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND MICROCALCIFICATIONS  NOTE  No ductal carcinoma in situ is identified  AXILLA  RIGHT   RESECTION  CARCINOMA METASTATIC TO 3 OF 16 LYMPH NODES  3 16   Diagnosis by  Jeoffry Brennick  MD Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 17 47 Consulting Pathologist s   Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS  BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinati