ormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  31 MAY 94 at 07 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a 6 x 4 x 0 6cm piece of breast tissue  with a localizing wire in place and accompanying x ray that shows microcalcifications  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma and fat  No frozen section is done  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A through P  Resident  Karen C  Deering  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST   NO LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA IS PRESENT  O R  Resident  Essam Ahmed  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Frederick William Ackroyd  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Negative.
