y submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remaining 3 nodes are entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remainder of the tissue is submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast additional inferior  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm breast tissue oriented by a stitch indicating the new margin  The latter is inked black  Entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast additional medial  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm unoriented breast tissue which is entirely submitted in block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Norma Rodriguez M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Norma Rodriguez M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Norma Rodriguez M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE Addendum note  An immunohistochemical stain for E cadherin shows strong positive staining of the invasive carcinoma  This result supports infiltrating ductal carcinoma rather than infiltrating lobular carcinoma  Addendum  2 by Kristina Br