Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  29 MAY 98 ACCESSIONED ON  29 MAY 98 at 14 04 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  SEE NOTE   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU IN THE REGION OF THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  NOTE  Focally  carcinoma comes to less than 0 5mm of the resection margin  No vascular or lymphatic vessel invasion is seen  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 26                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 04 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only and having an accompanying specimen radiograph are 2 fragments of breast tissue which are attached to each other in one area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm  respectively  The small piece contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm white  firm  stellate mass abutting the margin  The remaining tissue  including the larger piece  is fatty and unremarkable  A small portion of the mass is frozen as FX 1 and resubmitted as Cassette A  The rest of the mass is submitted in Cassettes B and C  Representative sections of the uninvolved tissue and the small portion in Cassette D and E  Representative sections of the larger piece in Cassettes F G  Gross Description by  PAMELA ROMAN Resident  RICHARD AMMER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN  O R  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  H  Thomas Aretz  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  David L Berger  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Positive.
