hat failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 21 17     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  46 fm mg cytosolic protein progesterone receptor  33 fm mg cytosolic protein Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 11 57 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  number and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fibrofatty breast tissue fragment with localizing wire in place and accompanying x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 3cm rubbery  tan nodule extending to within 0 3cm of the nearest inked margin  The remaining parenchyma is unremarkable  soft and white to yellow  The tan nodule is submitted in A  the area corresponding to the microcalcifications on the x ray submitted in B D  and the remaining tissue in E and F  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  number and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fragment of fibrofatty breast tissue  inked and sectioned to reveal a semifirm  tan to white  ill defined focus  measuring 1 5cm in greatest dimension and abutting an inked margin  Representative section is frozen as FX  1 and saved frozen  The rest of the lesion is submitted in G J  and the remainder in K M  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  NO LESION SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   EXTENSIVE  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA PRESENT AT MULTIPLE INKED MARGINS  O R  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD O R  Di