Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 AUG 94 ACCESSIONED ON  22 AUG 94 at 11 25 CLINICAL DATA  History of intraductal carcinoma in the left breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL ADENOCARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATIED GRADE REMOVED_DATE  95   REMOVED_DATE CM MAXIMAL DIAMETER AT SURGICAL RESECTION MARGIN  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  0 2  FIBROSIS WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS AND TYPICAL AND ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  Dr  Ferguson aware of diagnosis at 9 30 AM ON August 25   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Diagnosis by  James F  Southern  M D  Signed On  26 AUG 94 at 14 57 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding 